<title>UK: Rolls says aerospace unit sees work load hike.</title>
<headline>Rolls says aerospace unit sees work load hike.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering conglomerate Roll-Royce Plc said on Wednesday its aerospace group was experiencing a significant increase in work load in the current financial year due to a continuing recovery of the civil aviation industry.  </p>
<p>Addressing shareholders at the annual meeting, chairman Ralph Robins, however, regretted the recent problem experienced by users of its Trent 700 engine, mainly Cathay Pacific and Dragonair.</p>
<p>&quot;The problem is understood and a fix has been demonstrated. Modified parts will be introduced within a few days to allow their operation to recommence,&quot; Robins said.</p>
<p>Cathay and Dragonair suspended their flights last weekend after suffering inflight shutdowns involving gear box problems in the Trent 700 engines.</p>
<p>---London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
